WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.418 --> 00:00:03.001
(upbeat music)

00:00:07.210 --> 00:00:08.204
- Come on,

00:00:08.204 --> 00:00:09.650
(beeping) password.

00:00:09.650 --> 00:00:12.550
If you wear a mask and you
have an iPhone with face ID,

00:00:12.550 --> 00:00:15.460
you know this standoff very well.

00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:18.010
Except that might change for you soon.

00:00:18.010 --> 00:00:21.430
A new update to the iPhone iOS 14.5

00:00:21.430 --> 00:00:24.650
is going to have a special
face ID unlock trick.

00:00:24.650 --> 00:00:26.493
You just need one of these.

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:29.230
Yep, if you're wearing an Apple watch,

00:00:29.230 --> 00:00:32.480
your iPhone can unlock
without seeing your full face.

00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:33.330
How does it work?

00:00:34.630 --> 00:00:36.490
If your watch is unlocked on your wrist,

00:00:36.490 --> 00:00:39.830
and your iPhone is nearby,
but can't read your full face.

00:00:39.830 --> 00:00:44.560
Your watch will buzz and face
ID will unlock, and you're in.

00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:45.730
It's pretty awesome.

00:00:45.730 --> 00:00:47.660
Here's what's happening behind the scenes.

00:00:47.660 --> 00:00:50.640
Face ID tries to identify you as usual.

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:52.640
If he can't see your nose and mouth,

00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:55.940
it looks for your unlocked
watched confirm it's you.

00:00:55.940 --> 00:00:57.750
There's no actual scanning of your eyes

00:00:57.750 --> 00:00:59.800
or what's still visible of your face.

00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:02.483
See, even with my eyes
closed, it lets me in.

00:01:03.436 --> 00:01:05.570
How well does it work?

00:01:05.570 --> 00:01:07.590
Pretty darn well, other than the fact

00:01:07.590 --> 00:01:11.310
that you need to have an Apple
watch, which starts at $200.

00:01:11.310 --> 00:01:14.350
Talk about being masked in by Apple.

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:16.470
Let's do some speed tests.

00:01:16.470 --> 00:01:20.460
Mask free face ID, 0.8 seconds,

00:01:20.460 --> 00:01:23.540
face ID with a mask and
the watch feature enabled,

00:01:23.540 --> 00:01:25.433
1.4 seconds,

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:30.600
and a fingerprint sensor on
the iPhone SE, 0.7 seconds.

00:01:30.600 --> 00:01:34.540
Getting in with a six
digit passcode, a year.

00:01:34.540 --> 00:01:36.450
Okay, fine, three seconds.

00:01:36.450 --> 00:01:38.790
Worried about security and
someone getting into your phone,

00:01:38.790 --> 00:01:40.163
if they have your watch?

00:01:41.070 --> 00:01:43.930
Yeah, it can be done, but it's not likely.

00:01:43.930 --> 00:01:45.720
Each time you put on your watch,

00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:49.200
you turn on this whole auto
unlock feature on your iPhone

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:52.100
by entering your iPhone passcode.

00:01:52.100 --> 00:01:55.730
If someone has that, they
won't need your watch anyway.

00:01:55.730 --> 00:01:58.840
A bigger fear is someone
like mask man Kenny here,

00:01:58.840 --> 00:02:00.560
grabbing your phone and unlocking it

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:03.838
just by being close to the
unlocked watch on your wrist.

00:02:03.838 --> 00:02:05.220
What are you gonna do with my phone?

00:02:05.220 --> 00:02:09.160
- Tweets, access to her Venmo, sweets.

00:02:09.160 --> 00:02:11.360
- But Apple has some
protection against this.

00:02:11.360 --> 00:02:15.110
You can tap here to quickly
lock the phone from your wrist.

00:02:15.110 --> 00:02:17.240
In my tests, the iPhone and the watch

00:02:17.240 --> 00:02:19.740
have to be within 10 feet of each other.

00:02:19.740 --> 00:02:23.730
This is Beta software, so this
and other things may change.

00:02:23.730 --> 00:02:25.240
Plus this Apple watch shortcut

00:02:25.240 --> 00:02:27.500
is only good for unlocking your iPhone.

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:29.730
If you're wearing a mask
while trying to buy something

00:02:29.730 --> 00:02:32.430
using Apple pay, the app store, or iTunes,

00:02:32.430 --> 00:02:34.883
the phone will still
require your password.

00:02:36.130 --> 00:02:37.970
So how do you get it?

00:02:37.970 --> 00:02:39.993
Your iPhone needs to be running iOS 14.5,

00:02:41.100 --> 00:02:45.020
and your Apple watch needs
to be running watchOS 7.4.

00:02:45.020 --> 00:02:46.320
Plus you have to turn it on,

00:02:46.320 --> 00:02:49.720
by going into settings,
face ID and passcode,

00:02:49.720 --> 00:02:52.340
and turning on unlock with Apple watch.

00:02:52.340 --> 00:02:54.670
Right now those operating
systems are in Beta,

00:02:54.670 --> 00:02:56.800
and if you don't wanna wait
until the final release

00:02:56.800 --> 00:03:00.160
this spring you can sign up
for Apple's Beta program now.

00:03:00.160 --> 00:03:02.680
Anyone can do this, but
it's unfinished software.

00:03:02.680 --> 00:03:05.530
So there can be bugs or battery drain.

00:03:05.530 --> 00:03:06.920
So far so good for me,

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:08.653
but download at your own risk.

00:03:09.490 --> 00:03:12.813
Either way, this software
update cannot come soon enough.

00:03:15.593 --> 00:03:18.176
(upbeat music)

